            <div class="section-content">

                <h2>CHALLENGE</h2>

                <p>
                    Icons are widely used in mobile interfaces to create simple and efficient navigation. 
                    However, icons can also be ambiguous, particularly when users are unfamiliar with their meaning.
                    This project explored whether combining icons with text labels could make navigation faster 
                    and easier to understand in a public transportation application.
                </p>

            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- OVERVIEW / RESEARCH -->
        <section class="project-section">

            <div class="section-number">02</div>

            <div class="section-content">

                <h2>RESEARCH</h2>

                <p>
                    To investigate the impact of navigation style, I designed two mobile prototypes
                     in Figma. Both prototypes had identical layouts and content, but used different
                      navigation approaches: one relied on icons only, while the other combined icons with text labels.
                    The prototypes were tested by six participants across three everyday public transportation tasks.
                    <br>
                    <br>
                    Objective: This report aims to evaluate the effect of icon-only versus text-and-
                    icon navigation on task completion speed while users are either
                    walking or seated
                </p>

